  "_comment": "Shared test vectors for LiveHandshakeDirector (RemEx-8g6n0). Both the Kotlin and the C# director must produce exactly these decisions. Times are seconds on the splash clock; null means the event never happened. 'answers' are real probe answers ({at, target}); a link also counts as the target answering at linkedAt, and the target's effective answer is the earlier of the two. exitFromMark=true is the PC rule. expectAnswersShown lists the staged show times of answers shown before the hand-off, ascending. Tolerance 0.002 s when stepping in 1 ms increments.",
  "constants": {
    "floor": 1.4,
    "grace": 1.2,
    "cap": 3.0,
    "lockHold": 0.7,
    "exit": 0.72,
    "fadeExit": 0.28,
    "firstPulse": 0.32,
    "pulsePeriod": 1.0,
    "answerMin": 0.62,
    "answerGap": 0.18,
    "lockAfter": 0.5,
    "lineGap": 0.32
  },
  "cases": [
